out.push(A('⚠ **One count and it decides the cycle: how many students could produce the minute\'s own words for their decision?** **Four of ten.** **Six could not, and all six found that a decision they had been carrying for weeks existed as a sentence nowhere** — **so read two of the six aloud as they now stand and let the room hear what a decision sounds like when it is finally written.** **Then Mrs Rizk\'s ten past ten and her nine years.**'));

// ===================== 17.4 =====================
out.push(pb());
out.push(h2('17.4  Minuting a disagreement'));
out.push(S('Stage 1 · Get ready'));
out.push(A('**a** Open. ⚠ **Two sentences of about the same length, and no _however_ between them.** **Eight of ten first versions give the second position less room, and in six of the eight the shorter one is the position the speaker disagrees with** — **so write the twenty sentences on the board in pairs and have the room count the words, which takes four minutes and is the entire diagnosis.**'));
out.push(A('**b** Both parties would recognise themselves: **2** and **4**. ⚠ **2 has the same verb on both sides and the same document named.** **4 has the same verb and both reasons.** **1, 3 and 5 are a verb with an opinion in it, an _although_ that decides the matter, and a summary that records nothing** — **and _somewhat optimistically_ is the clearest example in the unit of a minute-taker taking a side in two words.**'));
out.push(S('Stage 2 · Listen and read'));
out.push(A('**a** **B** — ⚠ **the same grammatical shape, the same reporting verb and roughly the same length.**'));
out.push(A('**b** **1** ⚠ **It decides the disagreement.** **It tells the reader that the second position corrects the first, and in a minute of a disagreement there is no correcting** — **because the document exists to record that two reasonable people did not agree.**   **2** ⚠ **Each position gets its reason or neither does.** **A reason on one side only makes that side the reasonable one, and the side with no reason looks like an objection rather than a position.**'));
out.push(NOTE('⚠ **The word count is the teaching instrument of this cycle and it is crude on purpose.** **The real rule is the shared verb and the shared shape, but neither is visible to a student reading their own draft** — **and the length is visible to everybody, including the party who was given eleven words.** **So teach the count first and the verb second.** **Have the room count, then look at the verbs of the pairs that were nearly equal, and they will find _argued_ against _considered_ in two or three of them** — **which is the fault surviving the repair, and the room needs to see it survive.** ⚠ **And the diagnosis is more uncomfortable than it looks.** **In six of eight cases the shorter sentence was the position the writer disagreed with, and none of the eight had noticed.** **Say it as arithmetic and not as a moral point: a position you have not followed cannot be written at length, and you have not followed it because you disagree with it.**'));
out.push(NOTE('⚠ **The six words at the end of this cycle do more work than anything else in it: _could you give me your reason for the minute?_** **Asked after the meeting, of a party who gave no reason, it has produced a reason nine times out of nine in Mrs Oueidat\'s group** — **and three of the nine were better than anything said in the room, which is a finding about meetings and not about minutes.** **Teach it as part of the drafting process and not as a courtesy.** ⚠ **And insist on the second half: send each party their own sentence before the minute is circulated.** **In this class seven of ten sent them, five had a reply, and four of the five amended between one and nine words.** **That is an hour of work, once, and it removes the entire class of dispute that 17.7 is about** — **which is the strongest argument available for any practice in this unit.**'));
out.push(S('Language box · Practise'));
out.push(A('**1** **A definition** — _the branch considered the day-book to be a register for the purpose of regulation 11. The inspectorate considered that regulation 11 requires a printed register._   **2** **A date, with reasons** — _…because its cycle closes in November. …because the cold-chain line is rebuilt in February._   **3** ⚠ **A count** — **name the document under each figure and agree neither.**   **4** **A reason not given** — **neither side gets one, and you ask afterwards in six words.**   **5** ⚠ **One party senior** — **the same verb, the same length; rank changes nothing in a minute and that is the whole of its value.**'));
out.push(S('Stage 3 · Practise (sample – Card A)'));
out.push(SAMPLE([
  '**Row 1** _The branch considered the day-book to be a register for the purpose of regulation 11. The inspectorate considered that regulation 11 requires a printed register._ **Twenty words and fourteen.**',
  '**Row 2** ⚠ **The verbs decide it: _argued_ against _explained_.** **Replace both with _considered_, and the two sentences then differ by nothing but their content.**',
  '**Row 3** _The regional office considered October necessary because its cycle closes in November. The branch considered March necessary because the cold-chain line is rebuilt in February._',
  '**Row 4** ⚠ **_Claimed_ against _demonstrated_** — **the second implies proof, which is a finding the minute has no authority to make.**',
  '**Row 5** **The hardest.** ⚠ _The Aleppo bureau chief considered the figure to be twenty-six, on the regional return. The Homs bureau chief considered it to be twenty-two, on the desk log._ **The document under each, and neither figure agreed.**',
]));
out.push(S('Stage 3 · Practise (sample – Card B)'));
out.push(SAMPLE([
  '**Row 1** **Same as Card A row 1, and the room should say so** — **the two cards are the same disagreement from the two sides, which nobody notices until the fourth row.**',
  '**Row 2** ⚠ **The verbs again.** **A minute whose verbs differ has been written by somebody with a view.**',
  '**Row 3** **Both reasons, kept.** ⚠ **And if one party gave none, neither gets one and you ask in six words afterwards.**',
  '**Row 4** ⚠ **_Demonstrated_ is the worst word on either card** — **because it is true of the party who had the certificate, and a minute that says so has decided the item.**',
  '**Row 5** **Two counts, both honest, each on a different document.** ⚠ **Name the documents and agree neither figure, which is 14.1 arriving in a record.**',
]));
out.push(S('Stage 3R · Perform – listener task'));
out.push(A('**Rows 2 and 4 are decided by their verbs and the room names the pair in each: _argued_ against _explained_, _claimed_ against _demonstrated_.** ⚠ **Row 5 is the hardest**: two counts, both honest, each resting on a different document — **and the minute names the document under each figure and agrees neither, which is 14.1 arriving in a record.** **Make the room say what a minute that agreed one of the figures would have done, which is decide the item.**'));
out.push(S('Stage 4 · Your turn (sample)'));
