out.push(S('Stage 4R · Report (sample)'));
out.push(SAMPLE(['Mr Zahreddine chairs a site meeting at which the client\'s director sits, and for two years his action column was written after the meeting, at his desk, from his notes. Of forty-one actions in that period, eleven were not done, and he counted, which is how he knows, and all eleven had been written and none had been said. Mrs Khoury asked what the difference is, and an action written at a desk has been agreed to by nobody, while an action said in the room, with the name first, has been answered, and the answer is either yes or an amendment, and both are better than a line in a column the person has not read. Mr Attar asked about the name coming first, and name, act, date, and then stop: Mr Haddad, the figure with its denominator, by Thursday at noon, is that right, and then the silence, which is about three seconds and is the whole instrument. Mrs Oueidat asked him to say more about the silence, and it is the only part that cannot be written down: a chair who says the action and then carries on talking has let the room past it, and a chair who stops has made the named person the next speaker. Dr Qabbani asked about the director, and the same words and the same silence, with one change: may I put that against your name instead of is that right, because a director is being asked for permission to write something, which is a thing he can grant. Mrs Khoury said that is the only concession to rank in the whole unit and the room should notice how small it is: six words changed, and not the name, the act, the date or the silence. Mr Shihabi asked what happens if they amend it, and then you have a real action and you say the amended version back before you write it, and in eighteen months the amendments have been thirteen and the failures two, against eleven failures in the two years before. Mrs Rizk said thirteen amendments sounds like a lot of disagreement, and Mrs Khoury said it is thirteen pieces of information he did not have, arriving before the minute instead of after the deadline. Mr Tayara asked whether anybody refuses outright, and twice, and both times for a reason he would not have guessed: one man had no access to the system that produces the figure and had not said so in two years. Mrs Ajouz asked what goes in the column, and exactly what was said and answered, and nothing that was not. And Mr Zahreddine said the thing he will take away is the eleven and the two, and the only thing he changed was the order of six words and a silence of three seconds.']));
out.push(A('⚠ **The last line is the finding and it is the plainest arithmetic in the unit: eleven undone actions in two years of writing them at a desk, two in eighteen months of saying them in the room.** **The only change was the order of six words and a silence of three seconds** — **and the thirteen amendments are thirteen pieces of information that arrived four seconds after a question instead of on the afternoon of a deadline.**'));
out.push(S('Board clinic – typical mistakes'));
out.push(A('**1** ⚠ **No name** → **seven of ten undone actions.**   **2** **A department instead of a person** → **nobody in it can say yes.**   **3** ⚠ **The silence not held** → **everybody can say the sentence; nobody stops.**   **4** _I will make sure that gets actioned_ → **an action nobody can check.**   **5** ⚠ **An amendment not said back** → **the column holds what was asked, not what was answered.**   **6** **A refusal argued with in the room** → **the reason, which was the point, never arrives.**'));
out.push(S('Stage 5 · Read'));
out.push(A('**1** ⚠ **Forty-one actions with eleven not done, over two years of writing the column at his desk; thirty-one actions with two not done and thirteen amended, over eighteen months of saying each one in the room.** **They measure the same thing by the same method** — **and the only variable he changed was whether the action was spoken before it was written.**'));
out.push(A('**2** ⚠ **_May I put that against your name?_ instead of _is that right?_** **Six words.** **A director is being asked to let the chair write something down, which he can grant** — **and _is that right_ asks him to confirm his own homework in front of his staff, which he can only do by submitting to an examination.**'));
out.push(A('**3** ⚠ **Because somebody had to answer out loud in front of people.** **It costs discomfort** — **and the discomfort is the price of the information: one man had no access to the system that produces the figure and had not said so in two years, and nothing but a question he had to answer aloud would have produced it.**'));
out.push(S('Stage 6 · Write with help (sample)'));
