out.push(S('Stage 7R · Share'));
out.push(A('⚠ **One timed count: how long were the silences?** **Just over a second on the first attempt** — **so run it again with a watch and let the room hear three seconds once, and let it be uncomfortable.** **Then the seven undone actions with no name, and the four seconds it would have taken to supply one at the time.** **Then Mr Zahreddine\'s eleven and two.**'));

// ===================== 17.6 =====================
out.push(pb());
out.push(h2('17.6  The minute circulated an hour later'));
out.push(S('Stage 1 · Get ready'));
out.push(A('**a** Open. ⚠ **The interval, in hours or days.** **In this class they ran from one hour to eleven days, the median was three days, and two students had never received a minute of a meeting they attend** — **and the two are worth four minutes of the lesson, because a meeting whose minute never arrives has no record and every decision in it is whatever the most senior person remembers.**'));
out.push(A('**b** Belong in a minute: **2** and **4**. ⚠ **2 is a decision in the words that will stand.** **4 is an action with a name, a date and the two words _accepted in the meeting_.** **1, 3 and 5 are a discussion, a man\'s use of time and a mood** — **and the room should be asked who could act on any of the three, which is nobody.**'));
out.push(S('Stage 2 · Listen and read'));
out.push(A('**a** **B** — ⚠ **decisions, actions and positions where no decision was reached** — and nothing that was only said.'));
out.push(A('**b** **1** ⚠ **It makes the minute correctable by people who still remember.** **A correction at ten forty is _it was twenty-six, not twenty-two_; the same correction on Monday is _the minute is wrong_** — **and those are different conversations with the same content.**   **2** ⚠ **All three forms hide the person.** **A minute exists to say who decided and who is doing, and a passive in a minute is almost always a chair protecting somebody, usually themselves.**'));
out.push(NOTE('⚠ **The hour is the content of this cycle and the prose is not.** **A beautifully written minute on Thursday is worth less than a plain one at half past ten, because corrections arrive as corrections inside the hour and as accusations outside it** — **and the room will want to discuss style, so give them the arithmetic instead: eleven corrections in six months, nine of them in the first hour, and not one of them a dispute.** ⚠ **Then the striking.** **Have the room strike every sentence in the minute they brought that records something only said, and count the words before and after.** **In this class the minutes lost between a fifth and two thirds of their length, and the one that lost two thirds had gone out eleven days late** — **which is the cycle\'s two halves meeting: a minute written days later is written from memory, and memory supplies the discussion because the decisions are the part that has been dealt with.** ⚠ **Reading it aloud is the only reliable test for the sentences nobody said and it must be done out loud, not in the head.** **In the head every sentence sounds as though somebody said it.** **Aloud, the ones nobody said are audible** — **and the fastest version is to have somebody else read your minute to you, which finds them immediately.** **Mr Shihabi\'s example is the one to dwell on**: the sentence he could not remember anybody saying was his own, written in good faith, and it was the conclusion the call ought to have reached. ⚠ **Say plainly what makes that dangerous.** **A minute containing the meeting the chair wanted cannot be corrected by anybody without correcting the chair** — **so the people who notice it say nothing, and the sentence becomes a decision taken by nobody, in a document six people had no reason to question.**'));
out.push(S('Language box · Practise'));
out.push(A('**1** **A decision** — _Decision: the figure is published with its denominator in the same sentence, from 1 March._   **2** **An action** — _Action: the Aleppo bureau chief, the return for March with its denominator, by Thursday noon. Accepted in the call._   **3** ⚠ **No position reached** — **two sentences, one shape, which is 17.4.**   **4** ⚠ **Nine minutes that led to nothing** — **nothing goes in, and a paragraph says where it has gone instead.**   **5** **A decision you think is wrong** — **exactly as taken, with your view nowhere on the page.**'));
out.push(S('Stage 3 · Practise (sample – Card A)'));
out.push(SAMPLE([
  '**Row 1** _Decision: the figure is published with its denominator in the same sentence, from 1 March. The chair took this as agreed and nobody objected before the minute was sent._',
  '**Row 2** ⚠ **Not in the minute.** **Nine minutes at item 4 produced no decision, no action and no position** — **and a paragraph says that it is item 4 on Thursday.**',
  '**Row 3** _Action: Mr Haddad, the figure with its denominator, by Thursday noon. Accepted in the meeting._',
  '**Row 4** ⚠ **Not in the minute.** **_Wide-ranging discussion_ records that time passed.**',
  '**Row 5** **Two positions, one shape, no decision** — ⚠ **and the minute says that no position was reached before it gives the positions.**',
]));
out.push(S('Stage 3 · Practise (sample – Card B)'));
out.push(SAMPLE([
  '**Row 1** _Decision: the inspection follows the rebuild. Proposed by the regional office in the meeting and accepted by the branch._',
  '**Row 2** ⚠ **Not in the minute.** **_Three members said the form was difficult_ is a mood with a number in front of it.**',
  '**Row 3** _Action: the director, the paragraph on the audit, before the minute goes at eleven. He agreed to it being put against his name._',
  '**Row 4** ⚠ **Not in the minute, and _concern was expressed_ is the passive hiding three people** — **which is the worst entry on either card, because it looks like a record and names nobody.**',
  '**Row 5** **Exactly as taken.** ⚠ **The chair\'s view nowhere on the page** — **and the room will want a hint of it, which is the one thing a junior chair cannot afford.**',
]));
out.push(S('Stage 3R · Perform – listener task'));
out.push(A('**Rows 2 and 4 on both cards were only said and nothing goes in** — **and the room will want to record the nine minutes, which is exactly the instinct the cycle removes.** ⚠ **Rows 5 are the pair that matter**: one is minuted as two positions with no decision, and one is minuted exactly as taken, **with the chair\'s view nowhere on the page.**'));
out.push(S('Stage 4 · Your turn (sample)'));
out.push(SAMPLE([
  '**The minute I brought: the branch meeting of 9 February, circulated on the twentieth.**',
  '**Before striking: six hundred and forty words.** **After: two hundred and eighty-one.**',
  '**What came out.** **A hundred and nine words on the inspector\'s eleven minutes; sixty-two on what two members of staff felt about the forms; eighty-eight on a discussion of the day-book that reached nothing.** ⚠ **And a hundred words of mine describing the meeting\'s general mood, which is the largest single block and which nobody said.**',
  '**b** ⚠ **My partner stopped me at _the meeting recognised the pressure the governorate is under_, which nobody said and which I believe.** **And the interval was eleven days** — **which is why the minute was written from memory, and memory had kept the discussion and lost the decisions.**',
]));
out.push(S('Stage 4R · Report (sample)'));
out.push(SAMPLE(['Mr Shihabi circulates the minute of the morning call within the hour: nine thirty-eight to ten thirty, and it is two hundred and seventy words, and it took him four weeks to get it down to that, and the four weeks were about what to leave out. Mrs Khoury asked what the hour does, and it makes the minute correctable by people who still remember: a minute that arrives on Thursday is a document and a minute that arrives at ten thirty is a draft everybody can still check, and he has had eleven corrections in six months, of which nine came in the first hour after sending. Mrs Oueidat said and none of the nine was a dispute, and not one, and that is the point of the speed: a correction at ten forty is a man saying it was twenty-six and not twenty-two, and the same correction on the following Monday is a man saying that the minute is wrong. Mr Attar asked what is in the two hundred and seventy words, and decisions, actions with names and dates, and the items where no position was reached, and nothing that was only said, so nine minutes of a director talking is not in the minute at all unless it ended in one of the three. Dr Qabbani asked whether he was not offended at being left out, and Mrs Khoury said nobody is offended by being left out of a minute, they are offended by being summarised in it, because the director spoke at some length is a sentence about a man and not about a decision. Mrs Rizk asked about the passive, and it was felt that, concern was expressed, it was agreed: three forms and all three hide the person. Mr Tayara asked whether even it was agreed, and Mrs Oueidat said especially that one, and it is the hardest to give up, because it does not say who agreed or who was silent. Mrs Tarabishi asked how you find the sentences nobody said, and he reads it aloud before sending it, and four weeks ago he read a sentence aloud and could not remember anybody saying it, and it was his own. Mrs Ajouz asked what happens if a decision was taken that he thinks is wrong, and Mrs Khoury said it goes in exactly as taken and the chair\'s view stays out. And Mr Shihabi said the thing he will take away is the sentence he could not remember anybody saying: he had written it in good faith and it was the conclusion the call ought to have reached, and a minute that contains the meeting the chair wanted is the most dangerous document a junior chair can send.']));
out.push(A('⚠ **The last line is the finding and it is the most important sentence in the cycle.** **Mr Shihabi read aloud a sentence he could not remember anybody saying, and it was his own, written in good faith** — **and it was the conclusion the call ought to have reached.** **A minute that contains the meeting the chair wanted is the most dangerous document a junior chair can send, because nobody can correct it without correcting him.**'));
out.push(S('Board clinic – typical mistakes'));
out.push(A('**1** ⚠ _It was agreed_ → **who agreed, and who was silent?**   **2** _The director spoke at some length_ → **a sentence about a man that records he used time.**   **3** ⚠ _Concern was expressed_ → **a mood with nobody in it.**   **4** **An action with no _accepted_** → **a thing the chair would like.**   **5** ⚠ **A sentence nobody said** → **read it aloud; it is usually yours.**   **6** **A shade on a decision you dislike** → **the minute has become an argument and nobody will correct it.**'));
out.push(S('Stage 5 · Read'));
out.push(A('**1** ⚠ **_The chair took this as agreed and nobody objected before the minute was sent._** **It does not claim that the call agreed, and it does not use _it was agreed_** — **which would assert a unanimity nobody tested and is the form that is disputed a fortnight later in 17.7.**'));
out.push(A('**2** ⚠ **It names them and excludes them in the same paragraph.** **Nine minutes at item 4 on next quarter\'s staffing, which produced no decision, no action and no recorded position** — **and then where they have gone: item 4 on Thursday, by the regional editor\'s own suggestion.** **The nine minutes are out of the minute and the fact that they happened is in it, which is what stops a senior person feeling erased.**'));
out.push(A('**3** ⚠ **Corrections to the chair by eleven, and the corrected minute replaces this one with the correction named.** **The hour is what makes corrections cheap** — **and the word count at the end is there because a minute that grows past three hundred words has started recording what was said.**'));
