out.push(pb());
out.push(h2('17.7  Review & Mediate: a minute and the person who did not agree'));
out.push(S('Stage 1 · Get ready – Unit 17 quiz'));
out.push(A('**1** _…unless somebody tells me **otherwise**._ ⚠ **Delete _the_.**   **2** _May I **hold** that until item four?_ ⚠ **Delete _to_.**   **3** _…in the same shape, **and** neither party objected._ ⚠ **_However_ decides the disagreement.**   **4** _Nobody reminded **the room** that…_ ⚠ **Delete _to_.**   **5** _…it **would have been** done._   **6** _…in the room, **including** the regional editor._'));
out.push(S('Stage 2 · Listen and read'));
out.push(A('**b** ⚠ **That he had the minute and did not read it.** **It is true, which is why it is tempting: he had it for twenty-nine minutes and was driving for twenty-nine of them** — **and saying it tells a man that a deadline he could not meet was his own fault.**'));
out.push(NOTE('⚠ **This is the fourth mediation of Book 2 and the first in which the chair is at fault, and the room should be told so before the dialogue.** **Unit 14: nobody at fault.** **Unit 15: nobody at fault.** **Unit 16: an office that acted and did not write.** **Here: a chair who set a deadline of eleven for a man he knew was driving until twenty to twelve.** **The fault is small, mechanical and entirely his** — **and the lesson is that the formula of 17.3 is only as good as the time on it, because a route one of six people cannot use is a route for five.** ⚠ **Two answers for two questions, as in 16.7: the decision stands and the minute is amended.** **And the finding, which took a fortnight to surface: the dissenter\'s reason — that publication depends on the count being settled — is a position on item 1 and has never been put to anybody, because the only route for it closed at eleven on a Tuesday morning.** **Four people spent two weeks on whether he agreed and nobody asked what he thought.**'));
out.push(S('Stage 3 · Practise (sample – Pair A, the minute and the deadline)'));
