out.push(A('**1** **A**   **2** **B**   **3** **D**   **4** **C**   **5** **B**   **6** **C**   **7** **A**   **8** **D**'));
out.push(A('⚠ **Part 1 is the paper\'s first task and it is tested on collocation, not on meaning; a candidate who reads for sense and not for the fixed phrase will lose three or four of the eight.** **1 A** — _call a meeting to order_, **and no other noun takes _call … to_.** **2 B** — _take something as agreed_. **3 D** — _hold that until item four_; **_carry_ and _save_ are things you do to objects.** **4 C** — _a deferral that is not kept_, **against a promise, an appointment or a date, all of which are _kept_.** **5 B** — _set out_ the positions. **6 C** — _make an appearance_. **7 A** — _spoken before it is written_. **8 D** — _remind somebody that_, **where _tell_ needs no _that_-clause after _nobody told the chair_ and _mention_ cannot take a personal object at all.**'));
out.push(A('⚠ **The two to teach rather than mark.** **At 4 the candidate who chooses _taken_ has read _deferral_ as an offer; make them say what you do with a deferral, and the verb comes.** **At 8 the error is grammatical and not lexical: _mentioned_ cannot take _the chair_ as an object, so the item can be solved by a candidate who knows nothing about meetings** — **and that is worth showing, because it is how Part 1 rewards grammar in a task that looks like vocabulary.**'));
