out.push(SAMPLE([
  '**I shall take the first two points — authority outside the person, and agreement taken out loud — because both can be tested against a meeting next Thursday, and I shall not return to the third, which is a question about records rather than about chairing.**',
  '**The first point is the one that makes the rest possible.** **A chair of twenty-six cannot acquire rank by speaking firmly, and advice to be more confident is advice that cannot be followed.** ⚠ **What can be done is to rest every sentence on something the room can check: the time, the number of items, the number of minutes, and who is absent.** **_The people whose item it is are not here_ settles an item without anybody\'s permission, because it is a fact and not a preference.** **The cost is that the chair must then keep the clock, which is work.**',
  '**The second point is harder to defend than it looks and I take it for that reason.** **Taking agreement out loud, in the minute\'s own words, with a route and a time, is said to be a way of giving dissent somewhere to go.** ⚠ **It is, provided the time is one every person in the room can meet.** **A route that excludes one of six people is not a route, and I know of a case in which a correction deadline of eleven was given to a man who was driving until twenty to twelve** — **and a fortnight was then spent on whether he had agreed.**',
  '**Of the two, the first is a method and the second is a promise.** **The first costs the chair the clock; the second costs the chair the finality of the minute.**',
]));
out.push(A('⚠ **Part 1 is marked on the ground for the choice and on development, and this class loses marks by naming two points and giving no ground.** **The sample gives the ground in the first sentence — both can be tested against a meeting next Thursday — and uses the same ground for both, which is allowed and stronger than two separate ones.** **The third point is then dropped entirely.** ⚠ **And look at what the last paragraph does: it compares the two chosen points rather than summarising them — a method against a promise — and names the cost of each.** **That is the move that lifts a Part 1 essay out of band 3, and it is the same move 16.7\'s sample makes, which the room should be shown side by side.**'));
