out.push(A('**B  Listening.**   **1** **C**   **2** **A**   **3** **B**   **4** **C**   **5** **B**   **6** **A**'));
out.push(A('⚠ **Part 1 gives two questions on each extract and the second is almost always about an attitude rather than a fact; candidates who answer both from the first half of an extract lose the even-numbered items.** **At 1 accept only C**: _he says the number of minutes at the start and then again halfway through_, **and A is contradicted — he did not thank anybody.** **At 2 the key is in the woman\'s last turn, which is about the regional editor and not about the man she is talking to.** ⚠ **At 3 the bureau chief gives his own reason in one sentence** — _the reason I stopped is that he said the number_ — **and A is tempting because the request was in fact polite.** **At 4 the answer is in the third turn, not the second: he did mind the item never being reached, and he did not mind the tone.** **At 5 and 6 the woman names the half-hour and the man gives the remedy** — **and the candidate who chooses B at 6 has heard _the decision stays_ and answered with the thing that was ruled out.**'));
